Model Steel_and_aluminum_t
Title: Steel and aluminum tariff model
Description: This week, the US president has proposed a 10% tariff on all imports of Aluminum, and a 25% tariff on all steel imports, into the US. This has given rise to many conflicting claims about what the overall impact will be on our trade deficit and on our overall economy.~
~
We decided to apply a little common sense and quantitative analysis to estimate what the impact might be on the US trade deficit, after accounting for a few obvious secondary effects. This is intentionally simplistic, but meant to be understandable to everyone, as objective as possible (we, the model authors, have no direct stake in this issue, nor agenda), and something that you can put your own assumptions into.
Author: Lonnie Chrisman, Ph.D.~
Kimberly Mullins, Ph.D.~
Lumina Decision Systems~
http://Lumina.com
Date: Tue, Mar 6, 2018 9:45 AM
SaveAuthor: Lonnie
SaveDate: Thu, Mar 8, 2018 12:26 PM
