Chance degree_to_which_cost
Title: degree to which cost of goods is passed on
Description: In some cases, the increased cost for manufacturing may be absorbed by the industry in the form of lower profits, instead of being passed on in the form of higher prices. When the entire cost increase is absorbed, there would be no impact on trade deficit. This is a fuzzy multiplier indended to capture the degree to which the increased material costs are passed on the customers (0 = absorbed entirely by manufacturer, 1 = passed on entirely)
Definition: if Sector='Steel' or Sector='Aluminum' then 100% else Triangular(0, 50%, 100%, over:Sector)
